From: EEG-ZU3EG integration
Subject: [PATCH] gallium: expose the Xilinx display driver through kmsro

The project kernel identifies the display-only DRM device as "xlnx".
Mesa 21.2.4 already supports Lima-backed renderonly but does not ship the
xlnx loader alias or entrypoint. Keep the standard kmsro buffer-sharing path.

--- a/src/gallium/targets/dri/meson.build
+++ b/src/gallium/targets/dri/meson.build
@@ -88,6 +88,7 @@ foreach d : [[with_gallium_kmsro, [
                'st7735r_dri.so',
                'stm_dri.so',
 	       'sun4i-drm_dri.so',
+               'xlnx_dri.so',
              ]],
              [with_gallium_radeonsi, 'radeonsi_dri.so'],
              [with_gallium_nouveau, 'nouveau_dri.so'],
--- a/src/gallium/targets/dri/target.c
+++ b/src/gallium/targets/dri/target.c
@@ -118,5 +118,6 @@ DEFINE_LOADER_DRM_ENTRYPOINT(st7735r)
 DEFINE_LOADER_DRM_ENTRYPOINT(stm)
 DEFINE_LOADER_DRM_ENTRYPOINT(sun4i_drm)
+DEFINE_LOADER_DRM_ENTRYPOINT(xlnx)
 #endif
 
 #if defined(GALLIUM_LIMA)
